```rust
/// Parse dotenv-style `KEY=value` lines from a string.
/// Ignores comments (#...), trims whitespace, supports optional `export ` prefix,
/// and simple unquoted/quoted values.
pub fn parse_env_file(content: &str) -> HashMap<String, String> {
    let mut out = HashMap::new();
    for raw_line in content.lines() {
        let line = raw_line.trim();
        if line.is_empty() || line.starts_with('#') {
            continue;
        }
        // drop inline comment? The task says "ignore comments `#`" — I'll treat full-line comments; inline comments after values are ambiguous in dotenv. Actually dotenv files commonly have inline comments too. But values like `https://...` don't contain #. Many dotenv implementations strip inline comments only when preceded by whitespace. Keep it simple & safe: only full-line comments, plus strip inline ` #` when unquoted? The spec says "ignore comments `#`" — minimal interpretation: lines starting with #. I'll handle inline comments for unquoted values by splitting at ' #' — hmm, that could break keys with # in values (rare for API keys). Keep simple: full-line only. Actually let me support trailing comments after whitespace for robustness but document it.
        let line = line.strip_prefix("export ").unwrap_or(line);
        let (key, rest) = match line.split_once('=') {
            Some((k, v)) => (k.trim(), v),
            None => continue,
        };
        if key.is_empty() {
            continue;
        }
        let value = rest.trim();
        // quote handling
        let value = if (value.starts_with('"') && value.ends_with('"') && value.len() >= 2)
            || (value.starts_with('\'') && value.ends_with('\'') && value.len() >= 2)
        {
            value[1..value.len()-1].to_string()
        } else {
            value.to_string()
        };
        // skip inline comments for unquoted values: strip from " #" 
        out.insert(key.to_string(), value);
    }
    out
}
```

Wait — for inline comment handling, `.trim()` already removes leading/trailing whitespace, so a trailing ` # comment` would remain. Let me handle: if unquoted, split at " #"? Common dotenv libs (python-dotenv) strip inline comments. But a value like `sk-ant-abc#def` unlikely. But keys could have a `#` in password... For API keys it's fine. I'll support inline comments only when the `#` is preceded by whitespace, which python-dotenv does:

```rust
