Now the loading: read `.env` in CWD only, once (OnceLock), return HashMap:

```rust
static DOTENV: OnceLock<HashMap<String, String>> = OnceLock::new();

/// Load `.env` from the current working directory (only the CWD, no upward
/// walk). Parsed once per process and memoized.
pub fn dotenv_keys() -> &'static HashMap<String, String> {
    DOTENV.get_or_init(|| {
        std::fs::read_to_string(".env")
            .map(|content| parse_env_file(&content))
            .unwrap_or_default()
    })
}

/// Read an env var, falling back to `.env` in the CWD.
/// Precedence: process env > .env file.
pub fn env_or_dotenv(key: &str) -> Option<String> {
    std::env::var(key)
        .ok()
        .filter(|k| !k.is_empty())
        .or_else(|| dotenv_keys().get(key).cloned().filter(|k| !k.is_empty()))
}
```

